# Project Architecture

This project follows a structured end-to-end data engineering architecture to transform SAP financial data into meaningful business insights.

Data is extracted from SAP source tables and processed using Azure Databricks. The data flows through three layers — Bronze, Silver, and Gold — following the Medallion Architecture.

## Data Processing Layers

### 1. Bronze Layer
Stores raw SAP financial data extracted from the source tables without major transformations.

### 2. Silver Layer
Performs data cleaning, transformation, validation, and integration to ensure data quality and consistency.

### 3. Gold Layer
Contains business-ready fact and dimension tables designed for financial reporting and analysis.

### 4. Power BI – Visualization
Connects to the Gold layer to develop interactive dashboards and visualizations for business users.

## Dashboard Modules

The processed data supports four major analytical modules:

- **Management P&L:** Financial performance and profitability analysis.
- **Cost Center Performance:** Cost allocation and expenditure analysis.
- **Capex Analysis:** Capital expenditure and asset-related analysis.
- **Journal Analysis:** Journal volume, manual journal percentage, back-dated postings, and reversal rate analysis.

## Technology Stack

- Azure Databricks
- SQL
- PySpark
- Medallion Architecture
- Power BI

